The change made to the launcher base tree (runs/m1-desktop-010/pcie-m2-host-001/lab, not in git) on
12 November 2026, when the tip became the default. Kept as the record and as the way back
(`patch -R -p1 -d <tree>`, or the copy host_progress.py.before-tip-20261112 beside the file):
  - the member gate no longer requires org.puredarwin.kext.PDSun50iMMC, which upstream removed. A
    collection that has it (every pin collection) still passes: names starting org.puredarwin.
    beyond the required set are accepted, as before;
  - the console challenge is typed once the console has been silent for a second, in every boot
    (these are the hunks m1-boot-speed/launcher-fast-quiet.patch used to carry). At the tip the
    kernel no longer waits 30 s for a clock, the root mounts while the Wi-Fi driver still logs,
    and a kernel line inside the challenge's answer fails the proof (boot rb03).
Every per-boot launcher patch was regenerated against the new tree the same day.

